Cloud service types determine what service you get from the cloud service provider and what you in control of.
It will make sense when i explain the cloud service types. 

Infrastructure as a service
Infrastructure as a service is renting network infrasturcture from the cloud service provider. You manage virtual machines,
Operating systems, it is basically a whole local network accessed over the internet. The cloud service provider manages 
the physical hardware and datacentre security as part of the shared responsibility model.

Platform as a service.
Platform as a service offers the benefits of deploying code, applications and containers without having to manage the underlying infrastructure
such as the operating system, virtual machines or network access. You deploy applications and manage how users have access to it.

Software as a service
Software as a service you just manage access, no code deployment or underlying infrastructure management. 
